  "summary": "E-girls and e-boys, sometimes collectively referred to as e-kids, are a youth subculture that emerged in the late 2010s, notably popularized by the video-sharing application TikTok.",
  "description": "E-girls and e-boys, sometimes collectively referred to as e-kids, are a youth subculture that emerged in the late 2010s, notably popularized by the video-sharing application TikTok. It is an evolution of emo, scene, and mall goth fashion, combined with Japanese and South Korean street fashion.\n\nVideos by e-girls and e-boys tend to be flirtatious and, many times, overtly sexual. Eye-rolling and protruding tongues (a facial expression known as ahegao, imitating climaxing) are common.\n\nAccording to Business Insider, the terms are not gender-specific, instead referring to two separate styles of fashion, stating that \"While the e-boy is a vulnerable 'softboi' and embraces skate culture, the e-girl is cute and seemingly innocent\".",
